#: ../../source/capabilities.rst:145 d915afa5fb0f415c9c261d30df4e79a5
msgid ""
"`at_wall`, and the `Param` that a refused target returns. A clamp would "
"make an impossible command look plausible and the caller would never "
"learn; the status is the only channel a programming fault has."
msgstr ""
"`at_wall` ，以及拒绝目标时返回的 `Param` 。钳位会让一条不可能的指令看起"
"来合理，调用方永远不会知道；状态是编程错误唯一的通道。"

#: ../../source/capabilities.rst:147 e97fb0dfb11a48e897cb8e27f53fc55f
msgid ""
"`Param` for a target outside the window (the previous one comes back), "
"and for an inverted or non-finite window. A wall is *inclusive*: \"move "
"to the limit\" is the one command a soft limit exists to make safe."
msgstr ""
"目标落在窗口之外时返回 `Param` （上一个目标被恢复），窗口反向或非有限时"
"亦然。墙是 *含端点* 的：“移动到限位”正是软限位存在的目的——让这一条指令安"
"全。"

#: ../../source/capabilities.rst:149 1ed465c1251244c9b9b934b12bd4f48f
